// flat rate per room. Beyond Cleaning Group publishes from $50 per hour. TLB
// publishes neither a number nor a band, on a page whose only pricing answer
// is "we quote" - which is the honest answer and also the one a reader
// cannot act on.
//
// It stays SHORT and hands off on purpose. `end of lease cleaning cost` is
// 800/mo (workbook, 10 Aug 2026) and it belongs to
// /guides/how-much-does-end-of-lease-cleaning-cost/. A full pricing section
// here would compete with the guide for the same phrase and win neither.
//
// THE PRICE BAND IS NOT HERE AND IS NOT INVENTED. The rewrite brief drafted
// an opening sentence carrying "[Teagan to confirm: the price band for a two
// bedroom unit and for a four bedroom house]" and then said in as many words
// not to publish it with the bracket in. Both are right, so the section
// ships without that sentence: everything below is true today, nothing here
// is a number nobody has verified, and no bracket renders to a reader.
//
// WHEN THE BAND LANDS, it goes at the end of the first paragraph, in this
// shape and no stronger:
//   'A small unit in reasonable condition, empty, sits at the lower end. A
//    larger house that has been lived in hard, with carpets and ovens in
//    scope, sits well above it.'
// followed by the confirmed figures. Same request is open for the
// deep-cleaning page, raised 14 Sep 2026 - answer both at once.
const costBody: TextBlockBody[] = [
  'Condition and size set the price, which is why we quote rather than publish a flat rate. What we can tell you is the shape of it, and what moves it.',
  'Three things move a bond clean quote more than anything else. Whether the property is empty, because cleaning around furniture costs time twice over. Whether carpets are in scope, since steam cleaning is quoted separately and many leases require it. And the condition of the oven, which is the most time-consuming item on the list and the one agents check first.',
  'If you want the full breakdown before you talk to anyone, we have written it up.',
];

const costCta = {
  label: 'What an end of lease clean costs, in detail',
  href: '/guides/how-much-does-end-of-lease-cleaning-cost/',
};

// Section 9. Credibility signals.
//
// These frames are REAL TLB JOB PHOTOGRAPHS, published with the client's
// permission and with nothing identifying in frame — no house numbers, street
// signs, mail, people, or names on doors. That is why this section carries no
// "illustrative samples" note. Do NOT wire the `sample-` files back in without
// restoring a note that says so: a fabricated "before and after from a real
// job" is a false trust claim, not filler.
//
// ⚠️ BOTH PAIRS ARE KITCHEN SURFACES. The shower/bathroom pair this section
// used to carry was dropped rather than shown as an illustration next to a
// photograph, so nothing on this page evidences bathroom work. A real shower
// pair is the outstanding shoot; when it lands it takes slot 2 back.
//
// This is a DRAGGABLE COMPARISON SLIDER (BeforeAfter.astro), not the
// PhotoGallery grid this section used to be — the same change house-cleaning
// made and for the same reason. A grid lays four independent frames out and
// leaves the viewer to hold one in memory while looking at the next; the
// slider makes the PAIR the unit and does the comparison for them, in place.
//
// Shoot each pair from ONE FIXED POSITION. The slider wipes one frame over
// the other in place, so a shifted camera or a different crop reads as a
// glitch rather than as cleaning — a requirement the component cannot
// enforce and the brief has to.
//
// The photo brief. Both slots now carry real photography — cooktop and
// kitchen — so an oven interior AND a shower are both still outstanding, and
