//
// The alternative was to hide the module entirely until real quotes exist.
// Either is defensible. Holding copy wins because it keeps the section in
// the page structure, and because "we would rather show you two real ones
// than ten borrowed ones" is on-brand rather than apologetic - it turns the
// absence into the same position FAQ 2 takes about guarantees.
//
// STILL NEEDED, and this is the highest-value outstanding item on the page:
//   1. A tenant whose bond clean passed the exit inspection. The most
//      persuasive thing that could sit here, and the one thing the page is
//      not allowed to claim on its own behalf.
//   2. A property manager at an agency TLB already holds a contract with.
//      Written permission required to name the agency (BFD 5.3). An agency
//      voice answers the capacity and turnaround question a tenant quote
//      cannot.
// When both land, restore TestimonialCarousel with the real quotes and
