// shorter list) are flagged there, where one fix serves every page.

// Section 14. FAQs. Ten questions, one block, matching deep-cleaning.astro
// rather than the branded/non-branded split the older pages use. BFD 3.5
// asks for an FAQ block on every service page with self-contained 40 to 80
// word answers, which is what these are.
//
// EVERY ANSWER HERE IS DRAFTED, not briefed. The ones carrying operational
// numbers or commitments are flagged individually.
const faqItems = [
  {
    // [CONFIRM] the re-clean policy. Same fact as section 6, so the two have
    // to move together. If section 6 is deleted, delete this too.
    question: 'What happens if the property fails the exit inspection?',
    answer:
      'If the agent lists something that was on our task list, tell us and we will come back and put it right at no charge. That covers what we quoted for. It does not cover work nobody booked, or damage that cleaning was never going to fix. Let us know quickly, before the keys change hands.',
  },
  {
    // Deliberately does NOT promise a bond. See the file header.
    question: 'Do you guarantee I will get my bond back?',
    answer:
      'No, and be careful of anyone who does. Your bond depends on the condition report, fair wear and tear and what the agent writes, and a cleaner controls none of those. What we promise is the part we do control: the property cleaned to the standard the inspection is measured against, and a free re-clean if something on our list is picked up.',
  },
  {
    // BRACKETS REMOVED 15 Sep 2026. This answer carried two of them
    // ("[CONFIRM: half a day for a team]" and "[CONFIRM: a full day or
