    //    hard, runs to a full day or more.'
    // with the real figures in place of those. It needs a yes from Teagan
    // rather than new thinking - two numbers and this answer is finished.
    question: 'How long does a bond clean take?',
    answer:
      'Longer than any other clean, because every cupboard, track and oven rack is in scope. It depends on the size of the property and the state it is in, and on whether it is empty, which makes more difference than people expect. We give you a realistic window when we quote.',
  },
  {
    // [CONFIRM] the exclusions. Restates section 4b. Keep the two in step or
    // the page contradicts itself about what a client is paying for.
    question: "What isn't included in a bond clean?",
    answer:
      'Carpet steam cleaning, exterior windows, pest control, garages, balconies and outdoor areas, full wall washing and any cleaning at height are quoted separately rather than assumed. Repairs, painting, gardening and rubbish removal are not cleaning and we do not do them. Ask when you book if you are unsure and we will tell you straight.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Does the property need to be empty?',
    answer:
      'It does not have to be, but it should be. An empty property cleans faster, cleans better and costs less, because nothing has to be worked around or moved twice. If furniture has to stay, tell us when you book so we quote for the property as it will actually be on the day.',
  },
  {
    // [CONFIRM] whether TLB books carpet cleaning in or refers it out. The
    // answer below says TLB quotes it, which implies TLB arranges it. If
    // that is not true, this becomes "we will point you to someone who does".
    question: 'Do I need the carpets professionally cleaned as well?',
    answer:
      'Check your lease. Many tenancies specifically require professional carpet cleaning at the end of the term, and where that is in writing the receipt is usually what the agent wants to see. We quote carpet cleaning separately rather than folding it in, so ask for it with your quote and it is organised at the same time.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can you clean a property on the Queensland side of the border?',
    answer:
      'Yes. We work across the Northern Rivers, the Tweed and the Southern Gold Coast, so a tenancy in Coolangatta or Palm Beach is the same booking as one in Kingscliff or Byron. If you are moving across the border, you can book the clean at both ends with the same team.',
  },
  {
    // Middle sentence added 15 Sep 2026, so this answer points at section 8b
    // and at the cost guide rather than giving the same answer the page has
    // already given once. An FAQ that repeats a section verbatim is a wasted
    // slot.
    question: 'How much does a bond clean cost?',
    answer:
      'It depends on the size of the property, its condition and whether extras like carpet cleaning are included, which is why we quote instead of publishing a flat rate. The three things that move a quote most are set out above, and we have written a full breakdown of what a bond clean costs if you want it. Tell us the basics and the handover date and you will have a price back quickly, with no obligation attached.',
  },
  {
    // [CONFIRM] the product range, and the no-power scenario, which is an
    // operational claim about how the team turns up equipped.
    question: 'Do you bring your own products and equipment?',
    answer:
      'Yes, everything. On a bond clean that matters more than usual, because the power and the water are sometimes already disconnected. Tell us when you book if the property will have no power on the day, so we come prepared rather than turning up and finding out.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How far ahead should I book?',
    answer:
      'As soon as you have the handover date. End of month and end of quarter are the busiest windows in this region because most leases end there, and those dates fill first. If you are already inside a tight window, ring us rather than booking online and we will tell you honestly what we can do.',
