};
---

<Base title={pageMeta.title} description={pageMeta.description} canonical={pageMeta.canonical} business={business}>
  <SiteHeader
    logo={{ label: 'TLB Cleaning', src: logoImg }}
    primaryNav={primaryNav}
    serviceNav={headerNav}
    secondaryCta={headerSecondaryCta}
    cta={quoteCta}
  />

  <main id="main">
    <Hero
      variant="split-single-image"
      imagePosition="right"
      imageFit="contain-bottom"
      headingLines={hero.headingLines}
      lead={hero.lead}
      cta={hero.cta}
      image={hero.image}
    />

    {/* Trust bar + definition block share ONE photo behind a Cream scrim, so
        it is laid out across both. 75% keeps Dark Teal body copy above 4.5:1
        over the darkest part of the frame. */}
    <Backdrop image={definitionBgImg} tint="muted" opacity={75} focus="top">
      <TrustBar variant="card" cards={trustBarCards} />
      <TextBlock theme="muted" align="left" body={definitionBody} />
    </Backdrop>

    <PathwayCards
      heading={pathwayCards.heading}
      headingAccent={pathwayCards.headingAccent}
      cards={pathwayCards.cards}
    />

    {/* Heading rewritten 15 Sep 2026. Not one of this page's fourteen H2s
        contained the mapped primary (`end of lease cleaning`, 4,800/mo,
        Keyword Mapping workbook 10 Aug 2026). This is the section that does
        the most work on the page and the natural home for it, so the H2
        carries the phrase and "bond clean" moves into the lead rather than
        being lost. The six room headings underneath are untouched: the
        15 September audit found that list more specific than any
        competitor's in the set, and the specificity is the ranking asset. */}
    <ContentGrid
      columns={2}
      heading="What end of lease cleaning includes"
      lead="Also called a bond clean. Every cupboard, track and fitting, because that is what the inspection looks at."
      blocks={inclusionBlocks}
    />

    <Callout tone="note" body={exclusionsCallout.body} />

    <ContentGrid
      columns={3}
      heading="How the standard is actually set"
      lead="An exit inspection is not a judgement about how clean the place feels. It is a comparison."
      blocks={standardBlocks}
    />

    <TextBlock theme="light" align="left" heading="If the agent comes back to you" body={reCleanBody} />

    {/* NEW 15 Sep 2026, and it sits HERE on purpose: the invoice is what
        settles what was in scope, so it belongs immediately after the
        re-clean commitment that depends on it. See the CONFIRM note above
        `agentPaperworkBody` — this cannot ship until itemised invoicing
        and separate carpet receipting are confirmed. */}
    <TextBlock
      theme="muted"
      align="left"
      heading="What we give you for the agent"
      body={agentPaperworkBody}
    />

    {/* Theme flipped muted to light 15 Sep 2026. Not a copy change. The new
        block above took the Cream band, and two Cream sections in a row read
        as one section with two headings rather than as two. */}
    <TextBlock theme="light" align="left" heading="Both sides of the border" body={borderBody} />

    {/* NEW 15 Sep 2026. The three guides link to this page; until now this
        page linked to none of them. `list` rather than cards: three rows of
        title plus one line is exactly what this variant is for, it needs no
        images that do not exist, and the guides' own pages already use it
        for the same job. Copy and the reasoning are above `readingGuides`. */}
    <ServiceBlocks
      variant="list"
      heading="Before you book, three things worth reading"
      lead="We have written the long versions of the three questions people ask most before a bond clean. They are free, they are not sales pages, and one of them tells you when you do not need to hire anybody."
      items={readingGuides}
    />

    {/* Wrapper carries the #compare anchor PathwayCards card 3 links to.
        ComparisonTable takes no id prop, and adding one just for an anchor
        target isn't worth a shared-component change. */}
    <div id="compare">
      <ComparisonTable
        heading={comparisonTable.heading}
        cornerLabel={comparisonTable.cornerLabel}
        columns={comparisonTable.columns}
        rows={comparisonTable.rows}
        footnote={comparisonTable.footnote}
      />
    </div>

    {/* NEW 15 Sep 2026. Sits between the comparison table and the before
        and afters: the table has just told the reader a bond clean is "the
        most thorough of the three and priced accordingly", which is the
        sentence that makes them want a number. Cream, so the table above and
        the slider below both keep their own ground.

        Short by design, and it carries no price band — see the note above
        `costBody` for what is missing and exactly where it goes. */}
    <TextBlock
      theme="muted"
      align="left"
      heading="What an end of lease clean costs"
      body={costBody}
      cta={costCta}
    />

    {/* Drag the handle to wipe between the two frames of each pair — see
        the block above `beforeAfterPairs` for why this is a slider and not
        a gallery. Both pairs are real TLB job photography and the `note`
